{"id":"st2120-1","designation":"ST 2120-1","title":"Extensible Time Label — Structure","state":"active","suite":"2120","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2120-1/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2120-1/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"The TLX Suite is a multipart standard. This document is one part of the TLX Suite. The parts collectively describe a system for defining labels for elements of media content, representing the labels in various forms, associating the labels with specific elements of the content, specifying profiles of the labels for particular purposes, conveying individual or grouped labels over various connection means, and storing individual or grouped labels in various formats. This document part describes the architecture and data model of extensible time labels (TLX), the relationship to content, one specific representation in the JSON format, and general considerations for the design of applications of TLX Labels. SMPTE ST 2120-1:2026-03 Page 4 of 24 © SMPTE 2026 – All Rights Reserved","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 Terms and Definitions","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 TLX Data Model data model","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 TLX Representation representation","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.3 TLX Processor processor","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.4 TLX Encoder encoder","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.5 TLX Decoder decoder","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.6 TLX Application application","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.7 TLX System","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.8 TLX Profile","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.9 TLX Suite","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"4.10 TLX Label Sequence","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"4.11 TLX Label extensible time label TLX","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"4.12 TL